;; Command bare is a guest without a runtime (Arbace's, doc/go/BOX-NOTES.md, "go-whim vendored
;; whole"): the monitor's C guest, go-whim's guest/rt (hello.c, the faulty and read-ahead stand-ins
;; of guest_test.go and readahead_test.go, rt.c's calls, entry_ISA.S's entry and vectors) written in
;; Go's assembly (bare_amd64.s, bare_arm64.s) and built by Go's own assembler and linker, no C
;; compiler: GOOS=linux, linked at the monitor's image base with the entry _start (package
;; guest's Build: -E _start -T 0x201000 -R 0x1000). Go's runtime is linked in (the linker keeps
;; what its own roots reach) and never runs: from _start on, the code is the assembly's, and the
;; image defines no runtime/goos.RamStart, so the monitor lays it out as a C guest's (one vCPU, its
;; stack, the heap) and enters it as one (vmm/layout.go's plan).
;;
;; Its first argument chooses what it does: hello (the default) writes "hello\n" and exits 3;
;; null stores to address 0; deep runs its stack into the guard page; spin loops with no call;
;; ahead is the read-ahead stand-in (package guest's TestReadAheadBare).
(in-ns 'go.arbace.box.guest.cmd.bare) (go/file "main.go" :doc "Command bare is a guest without a runtime (Arbace's, doc/go/BOX-NOTES.md, \"go-whim vendored\nwhole\"): the monitor's C guest, go-whim's guest/rt (hello.c, the faulty and read-ahead stand-ins\nof guest_test.go and readahead_test.go, rt.c's calls, entry_ISA.S's entry and vectors) written in\nGo's assembly (bare_amd64.s, bare_arm64.s) and built by Go's own assembler and linker, no C\ncompiler: GOOS=linux, linked at the monitor's image base with the entry _start (package\nguest's Build: -E _start -T 0x201000 -R 0x1000). Go's runtime is linked in (the linker keeps\nwhat its own roots reach) and never runs: from _start on, the code is the assembly's, and the\nimage defines no runtime/goos.RamStart, so the monitor lays it out as a C guest's (one vCPU, its\nstack, the heap) and enters it as one (vmm/layout.go's plan).\n\nIts first argument chooses what it does: hello (the default) writes \"hello\\n\" and exits 3;\nnull stores to address 0; deep runs its stack into the guard page; spin loops with no call;\nahead is the read-ahead stand-in (package guest's TestReadAheadBare).\n" :imports [])


^{:go/end 17} (go/func main "main is never called: the image's entry is _start.\n" [])
